{
  "openapi": "3.1.1",
  "info": {
    "title": "Statistics API",
    "description": "The Statistics REST API: the request tracking of an Account. It reads what the dashboards show (Projects, Active Users, Throughput, Response Time, Requests, and Tags) and manages Projects and their API keys. Every call acts as exactly one User, in the one Account the credential is in now, with that User's full power.\n\nSign in with one of two credentials, sent as `Authorization: Bearer <credential>`:\n\n- **Agent connection** (`agentConnection`): OAuth 2 authorization code with PKCE at Auth, for the resource `http://localhost:13004/api`.\n- **Personal token** (`personalToken`): a `mvdm_pat_…` token a User creates on Auth.\n\nBoth are managed on [API & Agent Access](https://auth.test.local/User/AgentAccess). Every error is ProblemDetails (RFC 9457) with a stable `type` token. v1 only grows: a breaking change ships as `/api/v2/` beside it.\n\nSending Requests from a monitored app is not part of this API: it uses the Project's own API key with the `mvdmio.Statistics.Client` package.\n\nFor a walk-through, read [the REST guide](http://localhost:13004/agents/rest); to connect an Agent or the CLI, see [the setup guides](http://localhost:13004/agents).",
    "version": "v1"
  },
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/projects": {
